.TH passwd "" "Command"
.SH NAME
passwd \- set/change login password
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpasswd [\fIuser\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
passwd -- set/change login password
Usage:	passwd [ user ]
.HE
.B passwd
changes the password associated with a login
.IR user .
With no
.I user
argument,
.B passwd
changes the caller's own password.
An ordinary user may name only her own
.I user
to change her own password; only the superuser
.B root
may change another user's password by naming it.
.PP
Unless the caller is the superuser, or the account named has no
password yet,
.B passwd
first prompts with
.B "Old password:"
and checks the answer against the encrypted password recorded in
.BR /etc/passwd .
.B passwd
then prompts with
.B "New password:"
for the new password.
Unless the caller is the superuser typing a null new password,
.B passwd
rejects a new password that is too easily broken and reprompts until
a good one is given: the password must be at least four characters
long, or, if it uses only a single case of the alphabet (or no
letters at all), at least six characters long; it may also not equal
the account's login name.
.B passwd
then prompts with
.B "Verification:"
for the new password again; if the two entries do not match,
.B passwd
complains and leaves the password unchanged.
Any password given is copied into a fixed buffer of 32 characters, so
only the first 32 characters are significant.
.SH FILES
.DS
.ta 16n
\fB/etc/passwd\fR	password file
\fB/tmp/passwd\fR	temporary file while rewriting /etc/passwd
.DE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR login ,
.B su
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B passwd
complains and exits without changing anything if the named user does
not exist, if an ordinary user tries to change another user's
password, if the old password given does not match, or if the two
entries of the new password do not agree.
.SH NOTES
.B passwd
copies
.B /etc/passwd
to the temporary file
.B /tmp/passwd
while it works and removes the temporary file when done; if that
temporary file already exists,
.B passwd
retries a few times and then gives up with
.B "Tempfile busy, try again later" .
